 "method": "Dishub fixed plan, observed movements x per-approach scale.  Damped rounds s <- s (target/achieved)^0.7 overshot: near capacity an approach's hourly maximum queue tips from a short queue to spill-back past the 300 m camera, and it varies a lot between seeds.  The scales were then bracketed and checked over 4 seeds; an approach whose entry gates carry < 90% of the demand sent to it is capacity-limited.  W (RA Kartini) is capacity-limited: above about 0.38 its demand backs up upstream of the camera or spills past it, so its 155.5 m target is not reachable; it runs at 0.36 of the observed volume.",
